# Reference: keep MOST public (it shows the depth/complexity of the work).
# Only these buckets stay local:
#  - floorplans-maps: the school's blueprints + anything derived from them
#    (school security + architect copyright; one PDF is also >GitHub's 100MB limit)
#  - _archive: rough build screenshots + iteration junk (the unprofessional stuff)
#  - tools: bundled CLI binaries
reference/floorplans-maps/
reference/research/plan-pdfs/
reference/_archive/
reference/tools/
# real students' graduation photos — privacy, local reference only
reference/blhs-grad-capes/

# Build + map tooling: track the reusable pipeline only
scripts/*
!scripts/shot.ps1
!scripts/civil_extract.py
!scripts/build_campus_geo.py
!scripts/build_campus_dem.py
!scripts/build-campus-model.py
!scripts/build-pac.py
!scripts/palette_grade.py
!scripts/palette_grade_warm.py
!scripts/remove-bg.py
!scripts/bg-remove.py
!scripts/validate_feet.py
!scripts/render-campus.py
!scripts/pixelate-render.py
!scripts/normalize_tiles.py
!scripts/make_seamless_x.py
# the two files that prove the python runtime works. mp-spike.mjs was written,
# run and then swallowed by the scripts/* rule above, so the one thing the whole
# grape API rests on was never actually in the repo.
!scripts/mp-spike.mjs
!scripts/grape-proof.mjs

# AND THE WAVE GATES, WHICH IS THE SAME FAILURE AGAIN, FOUND THE SAME WAY.
# wave1-proof.mjs is the script BRIEF-ENGINE-2 calls "the pattern" and tells the
# next session to extend, wave2-proof.mjs is the run that proves this wave, and
# scripts/* had swallowed both exactly as it swallowed mp-spike.mjs. A gate
# nobody can check out is a gate that passed once, on one machine, on somebody's
# word. make-maw-standin.mjs comes with them because it GENERATES the bundle both
# gates run on, so without it the two scripts arrive pointing at nothing.
!scripts/wave1-proof.mjs
!scripts/wave2-proof.mjs
!scripts/make-maw-standin.mjs
# and the year one gate, for the reason written above it: seven of ENGINE-Y1's
# eight items live inside PmapScene, which has no unit test and cannot have one,
# so this script is the only thing that says they work.
!scripts/y1-proof.mjs
# and the dimwit run, which is the pass mark BRIEF-SELF-EVIDENT.md sets for the
# whole game: cold, 1366x768, mouse only, press the loudest thing. It belongs in
# the repo for exactly the reason written above the wave gates — a gate nobody
# can check out is a gate that passed once, on one machine, on somebody's word.
!scripts/dimwit.mjs
# and the arrival gate. Same argument as the wave gates and the same reason it
# had to exist: every one of BRIEF-ARRIVAL's eight items is a claim about a
# PICTURE, and all eight live inside PmapScene, the cutscene chrome and the
# published maps, where no unit test reaches. Twenty-nine checks, run against
# the LIVE deploy and the live published bundles.
!scripts/arrival-proof.mjs
# THE THIRD TIME THIS RULE ALMOST ATE SOMETHING LOAD-BEARING. vendor-islands.mjs
# runs inside `npm run build`, so swallowed by scripts/* it would be a deploy
# that fails on Vercel and works on the one machine that has the file.
!scripts/vendor-islands.mjs
!scripts/ending-fix.mjs
!scripts/play-harness.mjs
!scripts/surfaces.mjs
!scripts/road-shots.mjs
!scripts/travel-proof.mjs
# the first real island: the one that walks it, and the one that sails to it
!scripts/atc-island-proof.mjs
!scripts/atc-voyage-proof.mjs
!scripts/atc-walk-proof.mjs
!scripts/atc-tasks-proof.mjs
!scripts/atc-dock-proof.mjs
!scripts/atc-stamp-proof.mjs
!scripts/repro-brief.mjs

